       COUNT(*)
FROM Employee
WHERE COUNT(*) > 1
GROUP BY Department;

❌ Error


SELECT Department,
       COUNT(*)
FROM Employee
GROUP BY Department
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

✅ Correct


SELECT Status,
       COUNT(*) AS TicketCount
FROM Tickets
GROUP BY Status
HAVING COUNT(*) > 2;

SELECT CompanyID,
       COUNT(*) AS TotalJobs
FROM Jobs
GROUP BY CompanyID
HAVING COUNT(*) > 10;

. WHERE + HAVING Together

This is a favorite interview question.

Manager asks:

Show departments where employees earn more than 50,000, and display only departments having more than one such employee.

SELECT Department,
       COUNT(*) AS EmployeeCount
FROM Employee
WHERE Salary > 50000
GROUP BY Department
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

